Hmm, wait: what about `left.Type() == object.ARRAY_OBJ && index.Type() == object.NUMBER_OBJ` — for non-range single index it must stay. For ranges with index NULL (omitted in stepped), handle.

Let me restructure:

```go
switch {
case left.Type() == object.ARRAY_OBJ && (index.Type() == object.NUMBER_OBJ || (node.IsRange && index == NULL)):
    return evalArrayIndexExpression(tok, left, index, end, step, node)
